# {{PROJECT_NAME}} - Prologue Entry
# This is the first script the engine loads when the player starts the game.
# It introduces the project structure and routes the player to other script files using [goto].
# In a real game, you'd replace this with your opening scene, title card, or cold open.

@scenario {{SCENARIO_PREFIX}}_prologue_entry
@include {{CHARACTERS_INCLUDE}}

{{BG_DECL}}@label start
{{BG_START}}{{BG_TRANSITION}}[show lavender center {{LAVENDER_EXPR}}]
[wait 200]
narrator: Welcome to {b}{{PROJECT_NAME}}{/b}.
[show lavender center talking]
Lavender: You're looking at the {b}prologue script{/b} — the entry point of the entire game.
Lavender: When a player hits "New Game" from the main menu, execution starts right here, at the {b}@label start{/b} in this file.

Lavender: This project is organized into {b}story arcs{/b}: separate .vns files connected by {b}[goto]{/b} commands.
narrator: The arc structure for this project looks like this:
narrator: {color=#8888cc}prologue{/color}  →  {color=#8888cc}tutorial hub{/color} (16 lessons)  →  back to prologue
narrator: {color=#8888cc}prologue{/color}  →  {color=#8888cc}branch demo{/color}  →  {color=#8888cc}epilogue{/color}

[show lavender center happy]
Lavender: Below are two choices. Each one uses {b}[goto]{/b} to jump to a different scenario file.
Lavender: Open this file in the editor and read the labels below the choices to see exactly how routing works.

> Learn VNS scripting — 16 interactive lessons covering dialogue to release -> route_tutorial
> Branching scene demo — see how [goto] connects multiple script files -> route_branch

# ─── Route: Tutorial Hub ────────────────────────────────────────
# [goto] navigates to the tutorial_hub scenario's "start" label.
# The tutorial_count variable tracks how many lessons the player completes.
# When the player leaves the hub, execution returns here or ends.

@label route_tutorial
[set tutorial_count 0]
[goto {{TUTORIAL_TARGET}}:start]

# ─── Route: Branch Demo ─────────────────────────────────────────
# [goto] navigates to the branch_demo scenario's "start" label.
# That file runs a short scene, then [goto]s to the epilogue.
# This demonstrates the prologue → branch → epilogue arc pattern.

@label route_branch
[goto {{BRANCH_TARGET}}:start]
